id: pm-context-next-evidence
title: Plan the cheapest next reads for missing criterion evidence
description: "Choose which explicitly missing evidence to acquire from a caller-declared catalog, without executing reads."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: context,evidence,planning
created_at: "2026-10-25T01:45:14.508Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T11:26:59.940Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-25T11:26:59.929Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T02:06:36.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Three overlapping reads select the cheapest complete cover or disclose uncovered criteria; planning executes no read; revised source contracts invalidate the plan.; Typed SDK and CLI, compact JSON/TOON, typed remedies, docs, no-git real-data validation, targeted checks and npm/Bun CI release gates."
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-25T01:45:16.946Z",codex-agent,"Overlap checked against current CLI SDK/query, context evidence packing, pm-ops diagnostic plans and pm-rlm adaptive/evidence modules: existing packing selects present facts; operational plans execute approved fixed diagnostics; recursive workflows own model decomposition. This feature only optimizes acquisition of caller-declared missing criteria. Design: stateless exact bounded set cover with marginal coverage/cost ordering, revision-bound contract digest and explicit uncovered criteria. No imports, exports of native items, sync, claims, checkpoints, leases or outboxes are added; tracker state remains SDK-owned and untouched. Existing SDK stable JSON reader, expected errors and extension testing harness will be reused."
  "2026-10-25T01:52:13.269Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed stateless SDK and context-next-evidence CLI using SDK expected errors, stable packet reads and lossless table-cell encoding. Exact optimizer bounded to 12 criteria/64 reads; source revision contracts cover the full catalog and estimates; JSON saved-plan check rejects changes. Targeted planner tests passed 6/6, including 500 seeded sequences (2000 operations), full SDK-native state read-back with relationships, installed CLI with no Git, and five peer-transition boundaries. Registration/renderer integration passed 59/59. Public main snapshot validation: 91 items, 31 with criteria/tests, six selected items, seven missing criteria, three reads, one selected read, six covered/one uncovered; 523 estimated tokens + one call at 40 overhead = 563 vs 915 for the pair; JSON 869 bytes, TOON 912 bytes. Zero acquired reads and unchanged tracker fingerprint. Behavioral reverts rebuilt: greedy cover fails the three-read optimum fixture; bypassed revision refusal fails stale-plan tests. Restored before verification. Full release gates delegated to CI per the shared-host instruction."
  "2026-10-25T01:53:40.527Z",codex-agent,"Linked targeted run passed 65/65, with new planner native line/branch/function coverage 100/100/100. PM test-result tracking is disabled; the explicit run receipt was observed and is recorded here without changing tracking policy. Extended the seeded model to restore every plan through both JSON and SDK-decoded TOON, in addition to packet CRLF variants and SDK-native state comparisons. Existing local strict-health extension skew is tracked by pm-context-595f; isolated fresh CI health remains the gate."
  "2026-10-25T01:56:04.675Z",codex-agent,"Final expanded JSON/TOON seeded model passed 6/6 planner tests; targeted c8 confirms 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint, append-only history prefix and privacy-path checks pass. Fresh CI for implementation commit 516a388 has already passed strict tracker health, committed-build verification and type/docstring checks on Node 22 and 26; full npm/Bun release stages are still running. PR 176 is ready for review. Final full-gate run URLs and exact counts will be retained in the PR verification receipt."
  "2026-10-25T01:57:45.086Z",codex-agent,Full CI at 516a388 ran 409 tests successfully but the native aggregate branch gate refused 99.96 percent versus required 100 percent. The new planner module remained fully covered; the newly added command's default format branch was missing a direct handler invocation with an empty global-options object (the harness defaults differ). Added explicit direct default-TOON and global-JSON checks for both source and compiled handlers; the installed CLI regression passes. Thresholds and runtime implementation remain unchanged. Awaiting full npm/Bun CI on the corrected test head.
